## Upstream sources and their terms

This corpus is derived from public sources. Their own terms govern the underlying data and
are not superseded by the licence above.

| Source | Upstream terms | Use here |
|---|---|---|
| **Wikidata** labels | CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication) | Cross-script positive pairs, aligned by construction, and the pool from which hard negatives are drawn |
| **OFAC SDN list** (US Treasury) | A United States Government work, published for public compliance use. `[VERIFY]` current terms at <https://ofac.treasury.gov> before redistributing the extract | Cross-script and cross-romanisation positives from curated alias sets; the homoglyph finding |
| **Published transliteration standards** (ISO 9, GOST 7.79, BGN/PCGN, ICAO 9303, KMU 55, Uzbek Latin 1995) | The rule tables are published standards; the implementations in `benchmark/harness/translit.py` are original work under MIT | Synthetic positives with a known ground-truth transformation, capped at 30% of positives |

